SAM 3 video: run the per-prompt mask NMS in plain PyTorch when the `kernels` package is absent.

Upstream pin: transformers @ v5.12.1 (ddb849abe009d1089e6c691bfc897f27211c663c)

transformers runs SAM 3 video's greedy mask NMS through a compiled kernel that the `kernels`
package downloads from the Hugging Face Hub at run time (kernels-community/cv-utils). Without that
package it keeps every detection above the score threshold, so the overlapping duplicates NMS
exists to remove are all kept. This adds the same greedy rule in plain PyTorch -- the rule of the
original SAM 3 code's CPU fallback, generic_nms_cpu in facebookresearch/sam3 sam3/perflib/nms.py:
highest score first, drop any detection whose mask IoU with a kept one exceeds the threshold -- and
uses it whenever the kernel is missing or fails. The kernel path is unchanged when it is installed.
Hole filling and sprinkle removal, the kernel's other two jobs, are still skipped without it.

Without it: duplicates pile up frame after frame until associating detections with tracks runs out
of GPU memory, as it did on DAVIS crossing on a 32 GB card.

